+## Read the logs
+
+`docker compose logs --follow <service>` shows the log of one service as it is written. The names of the services are the ones that `docker compose ps` lists:
+
+```sh
+docker compose logs --follow reservation
+```
+
+The services write one JSON object per line. Without the prefix that Compose puts before each line, `jq` makes a log readable:
+
+```sh
+docker compose logs --no-log-prefix reservation | jq .
+```
+
